  "preamble": "Change of the voiced alveolar stop [d] to the voiced alveolar fricative [z]. It is the defining isogloss of the 'z-languages' of Siberian Turkic: Proto-Turkic intervocalic and final *d, kept as d in Tuvan and Old Turkic and shifted to y in Turkish, became z in Khakas, Shor and Western Yugur, as in *adak 'foot' > Khakas azax, Shor azaq.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Spirantization, Assibilation, Lenition",
  "languageExamples": [
